<title>CHINA: Shanghai offers low interest loans to listed firms.</title>
<headline>Shanghai offers low interest loans to listed firms.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai city government has offered low-interest loans to three major listed companies as part of its measures to support the stock market, the Shanghai Securities News said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The three companies are Shanghai Lansheng Co Ltd, Shanghai Diesel Engine Co and Shanghai Chlor Alkali Chemical Co, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not give amounts and interest rates for the loans and officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>The paper said this was the first batch of major listed companies to be given preferential loans and the city government would continue to give such loans to support the market. It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
